            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="0928" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/951: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bailly-Blanchard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-27T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 27,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:30
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>56. From McIlhenny:</p>
                <p>Department’s 68, August 21, 5 p.m. I have today requested the Government to
                    authorize the Receiver General to place to my credit <pb facs="0929" n="839"
                        xml:id="pg839"/> $2,250,000 to authorize me to convert this sum into francs
                    and with the proceeds pay interest and amortization now due. Requested that
                    French Government be not informed of my intention to pay amortization as under
                    contracts I am privileged to buy bonds on bourse below par to meet
                    amortization.</p>
                <p>If the Haitian Government complies with my request I will pay interest due at
                    once.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
